    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • The Volkswagen Group's Affordable BEV Quartet Has Almost Reached 150,000 Orders\nCadillac Unveils Escalade-V Checo Perez Edition and It's Limited to Just 11 Units\n9 photos\nPhoto: Cadillac\nCadillac's latest special edition model is an Escalade-V variant celebrating Checo Perez's return to Formula 1. The so-called Escalade-V Checo Perez Edition is limited to just 11 units, and they're all for Mexico.\nThis is an ultra-exclusive performance SUV, numbers-wise. And GM settling on just 11 examples is not your usual happenstance. In case you didn't know, '11' is the racing number used by Perez throughout most of his Formula 1 career. So, there's your connection.\nCadillac unveiled this special edition model earlier this week at the residence of the United States ambassador in Mexico, as Perez himself attended the event. According to the carmaker, Checo was personally involved with the project, from the design process to the official debut.\n\"Cadillac and Checo Perez share a passion for innovation, precision, and the constant pursuit of excellence,\" stated GM Mexico exec, Paco Garza. \"This edition celebrates more than 20 years of the V-Series legacy and recognizes the career of Checo - an icon of Mexican motorsport who has inspired millions of people, both on and off the track. The result is a truly exclusive offering for our customers, in which luxury, performance, and Mexican pride converge in a unique SUV.\"\nA quick look at these cars is unlikely to reveal what's special about them. It's only after a closer inspection that you might notice a few differences. For instance, each vehicle will feature two individually numbered plaques, one on the B-pillar and one on the center console. Both identify the production number (1/11 through 11/11) and Perez's signature.\nBuyers can choose between black and white exterior configurations, to go with contrasting black and white interiors - much like the livery of the Formula 1 car . Other noteworthy features include the black Escalade and V-Series badges, monochromatic Cadillac emblems front and rear, sports pedals, a visible carbon fiber V-Series engine cover, and special mirror-mounted projectors blasting V-Series graphics onto the ground.\nAs for the performance, the engine is completely stock and you get the same 682 horsepower and 653 lb-ft of torque as you would in any other Escalade-V .\nPhoto: Cadillac \"Mexico has always been with me in every race,\" said Cadillac F1 Team driver, Sergio Perez. \"That's why knowing that this special edition exists to celebrate that history makes me incredibly excited. I hope that the customers who own one of these 11 units enjoy them just as much as I enjoyed being part of this project - a project I was involved in from the design phase all the way to the unveiling of this special edition.\"\nTwo things. First, I'm personally curious why Cadillac went with the Escalade-V instead of something a little more... agile, like say the CT5-V Blackwing or the CT4-V Blackwing. If I had to guess, I'd say it's because they can charge way more for the Escalade-V, but ultimately, who knows?\nSecond, where's Valtteri Bottas' special-edition Caddy? Well, Cadillac doesn't sell any vehicles in Finland, officially; so that might explain it. However, Bottas is known to reside in Australia, where Cadillac sells the Optiq, Lyriq and the Vistiq, but more importantly, the Lyriq-V. They could make a special edition from one of those... just saying.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nCadillac Escalade-V cadillac escalade-v checo perez edition Cadillac Escalade escalade-v Escalade Sergio Perez Cadillac Mexico\nAbout the author: Sergiu Tudose\nSergiu got to experience both American and European car \"scenes\" at an early age (his father drove a Ford Fiesta XR2 supermini in the 80s). After spending over 15 years at local and international auto publications, he's starting to appreciate comfort behind the wheel more than raw power and acceleration. Full profile\nUP NEXT BMW’s i3 Touring Is an Electric Alternative to the Upcoming 3 Series Wagon – Spy Shots",
